470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (While both systems operate within the TARGET framework, they serve different purposes. SWIFT is used for global transfers, while SEPA focuses on payments within the European region. TARGET processes payments on a T+2 basis, meaning the transaction is settled either on the same day or within two business days, depending on the currency and time of the transaction. Additionally, the EU has developed TIPS \(TARGET Instant Payment Settlement\), an enhanced version of the traditional TARGET system, which supports instant payments, allowing transactions to settle in real time, although it comes at a higher cost.)
/E (While both systems operate within the TARGET framework, they serve different purposes. SWIFT is used for global transfers, while SEPA focuses on payments within the European region. TARGET processes payments on a T+2 basis, meaning the transaction is settled either on the same day or within two business days, depending on the currency and time of the transaction. Additionally, the EU has developed TIPS \(TARGET Instant Payment Settlement\), an enhanced version of the traditional TARGET system, which supports instant payments, allowing transactions to settle in real time, although it comes at a higher cost.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1601 0 R
/T (Securities Transfer. The European T2S channel processes securities on a T+2 basis. It is an EU payment platform created by the central authorities and several large securities custodians. Its purpose is to harmonise the transactions of EU and extra-EU securities. In short, this channel of transaction manages exclusively financial securities. Although the bond itself remains within the CSD, the T2S system is responsible for communicating the changes in nominatives within the CSDs. It is like if the CSD were the ledger and the T2S the person who writes and updates the ledger itself.)
/E (Securities Transfer. The European T2S channel processes securities on a T+2 basis. It is an EU payment platform created by the central authorities and several large securities custodians. Its purpose is to harmonise the transactions of EU and extra-EU securities. In short, this channel of transaction manages exclusively financial securities. Although the bond itself remains within the CSD, the T2S system is responsible for communicating the changes in nominatives within the CSDs. It is like if the CSD were the ledger and the T2S the person who writes and updates the ledger itself.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
