/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (MiFIR The aim of the regulation is to make markets of financial instruments more transparent, efficient and to give more protection to investors. The first part is related to the rules of the operations that happen in the market in order to provide transparency, efficiency and integrity to all markets. Negotiations must be taken into regulated and appropriate locations and new systems like MTF \(Multilateral Trading Facilities\) and OTF \(organised Trading Facilities\) are defined and regulated. Transparency requirements pre and post negotiations are introduced and the level of transparency is calibrated based on the financial instrument involved. Investment firms must provide clear and complete details about operations to competent authorities \(ESMA, ABE, National Authorities\) as quickly as possible, at the latest at the end of the following working day. Reports of the operations comprehend: identification of the instruments, quantity, price, date/time, identification of the clients, of who made the investment decision and of who executed it. These reports are crucial to make competent authorities able to monitor the activities of investment firms. Trading venues must keep data of every negotiation happened for at least five years in order to be available to competent authorities. Regarding investors protection, issuers of financial instruments must provide information periodically, this information  includes  identifying  details,  services  and  investment  activities,  customers )
/E (MiFIR The aim of the regulation is to make markets of financial instruments more transparent, efficient and to give more protection to investors. The first part is related to the rules of the operations that happen in the market in order to provide transparency, efficiency and integrity to all markets. Negotiations must be taken into regulated and appropriate locations and new systems like MTF \(Multilateral Trading Facilities\) and OTF \(organised Trading Facilities\) are defined and regulated. Transparency requirements pre and post negotiations are introduced and the level of transparency is calibrated based on the financial instrument involved. Investment firms must provide clear and complete details about operations to competent authorities \(ESMA, ABE, National Authorities\) as quickly as possible, at the latest at the end of the following working day. Reports of the operations comprehend: identification of the instruments, quantity, price, date/time, identification of the clients, of who made the investment decision and of who executed it. These reports are crucial to make competent authorities able to monitor the activities of investment firms. Trading venues must keep data of every negotiation happened for at least five years in order to be available to competent authorities. Regarding investors protection, issuers of financial instruments must provide information periodically, this information  includes  identifying  details,  services  and  investment  activities,  customers )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
