/T (This Regime completely replaced the previous Market Abuse Directive of 2003. The aim of the MAR and CSMAD is to ensure greater transparency and market integrity. MAR introduces some changes like notification requirements in relation to suspicious activities or delay in disclosure of inside information; enhance requirements regarding the preparation of insider lists and handling of inside information. The CSMAD introduces the definition of a wider range of activities that constitute an offence or a market abuse and minimum rules for criminal sanctions related to market abuse are introduced. )
