/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
759 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Euronext acts as a central authority and network regulator, with the main functions of:)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
760 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1715 0 R
/E (Validator and gatekeeper, as it approves and verify the onboarding on the blockchain of all the different actors \(issuers, regulators, financial authorities, retail and institutional investors\), ensuring compliance with all regulations. In particular, the gatekeeper function of Euronext would be critical to grant different roles and access levels to the different participants of the network, distinguishing between the different actors and the functions they will cover in the blockchain.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
761 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1716 0 R
/E (Network manager, as it oversees network governance, updates protocol rules and coordinates with the financial authorities when needed.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
762 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1717 0 R
/E (Transaction ledger maintenance, as it must check and approve the transactions record and to ensure integrity, authenticity and immutability of the ledger over time.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
763 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
