1033 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Additionally, the choice between single-chain architectures and cross-chain or multi-chain infrastructures can affect overall energy consumption. On one side, individual blockchain, especially if based on efficient consensus mechanism, are generally not energy intensive, on the other side platforms that incorporate multiple blockchain can show additional energy consumption. This overhead is due to the multiple node infrastructures, the validating cross-network transactions, and operating interoperability protocols or bridges. However, the increase is marginal if across the network energy-efficient consensus algorithms are used. Furthermore cross-chain solutions offer enhanced scalability, modularity, and the ability to allocate tasks to the most appropriate and energy-efficient chain, optimising resource allocation. Therefore, the total energy footprint may be slightly higher but the environmental impact remains low. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
