/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The report proposes a general methodology for calculating the carbon footprint of a financial product tokenised on the Ethereum public blockchain infrastructure, considering the entire life cycle of a digital bond, from its issuance and management \(including corporate actions\) to its final redemption, on the blockchain. A key finding is that the carbon footprint of a digital bond for its entire life cycle on the blockchain is 0.82 kg CO2. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1052 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (It is important to notice that GHG emissions related to the usage of the Ethereum network remain low compared to generic cloud infrastructures: the main part of the energy consumption comes from SG Forge's dedicated infrastructure \(cloud services and node services\).)
/Pg 46 0 R
>>
endobj
